# Supabase CLI runtime caches — never committed.
# These files are written by `supabase start` / `supabase link` and
# contain either service versions (no secrets) or project linkage
# metadata (project_ref points at whichever Supabase Cloud project
# was last linked -- could be production).
#
# The local stack reads config.toml only; .temp/ is incidental.
#
# IMPORTANT: If you've ever run `supabase link --project-ref <id>` on
# this machine, the linked-project.json file in .temp/ will contain
# a project_ref. That file is local-only and does NOT cause the
# local stack to touch production, but committing it would expose
# which Supabase orgs/projects you work with. Treat .temp/ as
# local-only state.

.temp/
